---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Beau" description="Beau is a fully vaccinated orange kitten, and the biggest little piggy around, ready to find his forever home with Lucky Penny Kitties.">
  <section class="section cat-profile">
    <div class="cat-profile-header">
      <h1>Beau</h1>
      <span class="badge">Male</span>
      <span id="cat-badge" class="badge" hidden></span>
    </div>

    <p class="cat-age">3 months old</p>

    <p class="cat-tagline">
      Beau (grey collar) is also the biggest piggy and always the last one
      left eating once everyone else is done. Very affectionate.
    </p>

    <div class="cat-gallery">
      <img src="/cats/beau-1.webp" alt="Beau the kitten" loading="lazy" />
      <img src="/cats/beau-2.webp" alt="Beau the kitten" loading="lazy" />
      <img src="/cats/beau-3.webp" alt="Beau the kitten" loading="lazy" />
      <img src="/cats/beau-4.webp" alt="Beau the kitten" loading="lazy" />
      <img src="/cats/beau-5.webp" alt="Beau the kitten" loading="lazy" />
    </div>

    <p class="cat-bio">
      Beau was born in May of 2026 and is a fully vaccinated orange kitten
      who's ready to find his forever home!
    </p>

    <p class="cat-bio">
      Beau and Chandler are identical twin brothers. They'd make an adorable
      pair if adopted together, but Beau is confident enough to thrive in a
      home of his own, too.
    </p>

    <p class="cat-bio">
      Beau (gray collar) is the biggest little piggy around! &#127869;&#65039;
      He's always the last one at the food bowl after everyone else has
      finished, and once he's full, he's incredibly affectionate. Just like
      his brother, Beau has never met a stranger!
    </p>

    <p class="cat-bio">
      Is Beau the missing piece to your family? &#128062;
    </p>
  </section>

  <script>
    interface Cat {
      name: string;
      breed: string;
      age: string;
      sex: string;
      status: string;
    }

    async function loadStatus() {
      try {
        const res = await fetch('/api/cats');
        if (!res.ok) return;
        const cats: Cat[] = await res.json();
        const cat = cats.find(c => c.name === 'Beau');
        if (!cat) return;

        const badge = document.getElementById('cat-badge');
        if (badge && cat.status) {
          badge.textContent = cat.status;
          badge.hidden = false;
        }
      } catch (err) {
        console.error(err);
      }
    }

    loadStatus();
  </script>
</Layout>
